0 < 1 #!/usr/bin/env bun
2 > 1 // Jev arranges the whole page from what the app can do, before any story names a
3 < 1 // control. The candidates come from the cards and the store by code, never from a
4 < 1 // story's `ui` or `see`: each card action's control (a bound ActionButton or
6 > 1 // ActionCheckbox, its words the action's `label`; an action taking rows of two tables an
7 < 1 // ActionSelect in the first table's list, picking a row of the second, narrowed by that
9 > 1 // input's `x-where`), each string input's DraftInput and each number input's DraftNumber (its words the
10 < 1 // input's `x-label`),
8 < 2 // input's `x-where`), each string input's DraftInput (its words the input's `x-label`),
9 < 1 // one list per table its row actions work on, a few
5 < 2 // ActionCheckbox, its words the action's `label`), each string input's DraftInput (its
6 < 2 // words the input's `x-label`), one list per table its row actions work on, a few
8 > 1 // containers, the page title and each card's purpose, and each card's `shows` lines: a
9 < 1 // row line a Text in its table's list row, before the row's controls; a page line a Text
10 < 1 // and a heading line a level-1 Heading outside the lists (a heading line takes the page
11 < 1 // title's place), their slots filled by `format` from cells, values, `sum` and `count`,
12 < 1 // in the card's `words` where it gives them. Jev only chooses and places them,
7 < 2 // containers, the page title and each card's purpose. Jev only chooses and places them,
8 < 1 // through json-render's composer, once per version of questions.json's authoring_arrange.
1 < 2 // Jev arranges each piece's screen from what the app can do. The candidates come
2 < 2 // from the bundle by code: every control a story's `ui` step names (a bound
3 < 2 // DraftInput, a bound ActionButton, a list of a table's rows), a few containers,
4 < 2 // the page title and the card's purpose. Jev only chooses and places them, through
5 < 2 // json-render's composer, once per version of questions.json's authoring_arrange.
6 < 1 // The kit is the installed TinyApp's: its catalog and store, and the composer copied
7 < 1 // to <app>/.preview/json-render/ so it shares the app's zod.
8 < 1 //
10 > 1 //   bun skills/ultrawrite/stories/arrange.ts <bundle> --app <dir>              writes screens/screen.<V>.json
11 < 1 //   bun skills/ultrawrite/stories/arrange.ts <bundle> --app <dir> --pick <V>   copies it to screens/screen.json
12 < 1 //   bun skills/ultrawrite/stories/arrange.ts <bundle> --app <dir> --reshape --note <text> [--note <text>...]
9 < 2 //   bun skills/ultrawrite/stories/arrange.ts <bundle> --app <dir> [--piece <piece>]
10 < 2 //   bun skills/ultrawrite/stories/arrange.ts <bundle> --app <dir> --piece <p> --pick <V>
